    "body": "Code quality finding #3230 flagged an unreachable defensive guard in `modules/adswagBidAdapter.ts` — `if (DEFAULT_ENDPOINT === null) return true;` inside `isPermittedEndpoint()` — which could never fire because `DEFAULT_ENDPOINT` was always a string constant in the actual build.\n\n## Investigation\n\n- Confirmed the finding's exact location (line 427, cols 7–32) matches `if (DEFAULT_ENDPOINT === null) return true;` from an earlier version of the file (commit `1c2fb778e`, \"New bid adapter: Adswag\").\n- Traced the dead code to commit `e9c63dd1d` (\"Adswag Bid Adapter: drop self-distributed endpoint variant scaffolding\"), already present in this branch's base, which removed exactly this guard along with the related unreachable `if (!isNonEmptyStr(endpoint))` branch in `groupBids()` — both made moot once `DEFAULT_ENDPOINT` was simplified to a plain non-nullable string.\n- Verified via `grep` that no `DEFAULT_ENDPOINT === null` or similar dead guard remains in the current file.\n\n## Outcome\n\nNo code changes are included — the flagged condition was already eliminated by a prior commit in this branch's history before this task began.",
